Z||000000||Return of Fiero||10-21-2001||04:28 PM||||just a question about elcrical. i have decided to ASS-U-ME that the problem with my 84 2M4 is the main engine wiring harness, due to signs let by a past Fiero of mine. the ECM blew up and my 88 2.5, and the car decided it would alow me to use the electric components (lights, radio ,locks ,etc.) but it wouldn't turn over. the car went into the norm, right till it was suposed to to kick in the starter (later i found the fuel pump wasnt woring, and that when i figured it was ECM.) now my 84 is doing it, and the wires look a bit...... melted? when i turn the key to the on position, everything is normal, but the fuel pump. doesnt turn on. then when i turn it to start the audio (not the radio) turns off, and the lights dim. the starter and sylaniod don't not engage. they do work, as i have "hot wired" the starter sylanoid and we have cranking. does it seem logical to say it IS the harness? or did i make an ass out of myself having the part shiped from cali to new england?<BR>OH, and also, can some one tell me what wires are suposed to go to the sylanoid, the color, the terminal they go to, and where they come from, and any fusibal links that are suposed to be there? looks like the last owner did a quick hack job on it when he ground out the starter. sorry so long, thanks||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||10-21-2001||05:21 PM||||Next time you want wire or anything else, try Kickhill.com they are in conecticut as I recall.<P>Melted wires are never a good sign. Best to replace repair that ASAP.<P>Check the stuff in the wire service article in my cave. Since this is an 84, also check carefully on/around the starter for toasted/damaged/loose wires.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Return of Fiero||10-21-2001||07:46 PM||||before you read, realize i like to make wise cracks/jokes about stuff, (ask list members from fierolist.<BR>as stated, the wires around the starter have been "hacked" in, there for i need the wire colors, and the "original" starting and ending point of the wires so i can keep my fiero from becomeing a burning lawn ornament.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>other than the wires path, and colors, i was wondering if i guessed right about the toasted wire harness. it kind of look like a burn marshmellow.<BR>thank you for your reassurance,though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
